WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.650
- Okay, so what about your childhood?

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.390
What's like a favorite Christmas memory?

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.040
- Oh, favorite Christmas memory.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.400
I remember one year, because
of me, it was my bright idea.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.350
I'm the creative in the family.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.037
And I put together, I was like,

00:00:12.037 --> 00:00:15.240
"Let's have a family talent show."

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.080
- Yes!

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.300
- And so, I thought I was gonna win,

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.239
because you know, I'm
the talent of the family.

00:00:20.239 --> 00:00:21.120
(audience laughing)

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.303
And I sang "Angel" by-

00:00:25.989 --> 00:00:27.090
♪ Angel ♪

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:27.957
- [Audience Member] Anita Baker.

00:00:27.957 --> 00:00:28.790
- Anita Baker!

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:29.623
God, drew a blank!

00:00:29.623 --> 00:00:30.456
Thanks!

00:00:30.456 --> 00:00:32.070
And then my uncles came in

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.040
and they blew the roof off the house with

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.480
the Temptations song.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.620
- Oh, which one?

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.947
- Um...

00:00:38.947 --> 00:00:41.483
(in deep voice) ♪ It's Merry
Christmas. Happy New Year♪

00:00:41.483 --> 00:00:43.290
Because I have an uncle with the-

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.510
why can't I think of songs today?

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.512
Say that again.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:47.345
- [Audience Member 2] "Silent Night".

00:00:47.345 --> 00:00:48.178
- "Silent Night", yes!

00:00:48.178 --> 00:00:49.080
"Silent Night".

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.160
- No one's ever heard of it.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.020
- No. Right. That's a, that's a new,

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.546
it's a new song, apparently.

00:00:53.546 --> 00:00:54.571
(audience laughing)

00:00:54.571 --> 00:00:55.404
- So they, they kicked your behind.

00:00:55.404 --> 00:00:56.237
- [Taraji] The killed it.

00:00:56.237 --> 00:00:57.120
They totally stole the show.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.130
And it's literally, we
talk about it to this day.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.170
I mean, this was when I was 12.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:03.390
I'm 53. We're still
talking about this moment.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.223
- Oh God, wait!

00:01:04.223 --> 00:01:05.056
Wait.

00:01:05.056 --> 00:01:06.030
I totally thought you meant you did this

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.428
as an adult and you were like-

00:01:07.428 --> 00:01:08.261
- No!

00:01:08.261 --> 00:01:09.120
- And you were like, "I wanted everyone

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.619
to do a talent show
'cause I was gonna win."

00:01:10.619 --> 00:01:11.452
- I did.

00:01:11.452 --> 00:01:12.960
- And I was like, I was just
picturing you at like 35.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.976
Just like, "I've got my Anita Baker".

00:01:14.976 --> 00:01:15.809
(Taraji laughing)

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:16.642
- No!

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:17.475
- [Kelly] Okay. I love it.

00:01:17.475 --> 00:01:18.780
It's even, it would've been
better if you would've been 35.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:19.613
(audience laughing)

00:01:19.613 --> 00:01:20.446
So what's one of your

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:21.279
favorite Christmas memories with your son?

00:01:21.279 --> 00:01:22.112
- [Taraji] Oh God.

00:01:22.112 --> 00:01:23.688
- He's older now, but like did he get-

00:01:23.688 --> 00:01:26.910
- No, he is grown now, but I
loved when they're little bits.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.792
- You know, when they're
little, little, little, because-

00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:29.625
(audience sighing in happiness)

00:01:29.625 --> 00:01:30.540
But you know, that's my baby.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.800
He's so grown now,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.087
and that was, I produced
that play on Broadway.

00:01:34.087 --> 00:01:36.313
"Jaja's African Hair Braiding" yeah.

00:01:36.313 --> 00:01:37.146
(Kelly and audience applauding)

00:01:37.146 --> 00:01:37.979
(Taraji giggling)

00:01:37.979 --> 00:01:38.812
- [Kelly} That's awesome.

00:01:38.812 --> 00:01:39.645
That's so awesome to
see his mama killing it.

00:01:39.645 --> 00:01:40.478
- Yes!

00:01:40.478 --> 00:01:41.311
He was so proud.

00:01:41.311 --> 00:01:42.360
He really was proud.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.890
- It is. I have the young age still,

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:44.971
so it is kind of still fun.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:45.804
- [Taraji] It's fun!

00:01:45.804 --> 00:01:47.460
- Because, you know,

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.110
I think we have more fun than they do,

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.960
like putting the toys
together the night before.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.280
But my son was funny.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.200
He liked what he liked.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.480
So he would pick like two or three things.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.307
I swear, I think I picked the
wrong baby up at the hospital.

00:02:00.307 --> 00:02:01.140
(audience laughing)

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.720
But he would pick like four
toys and that's all he wanted.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.827
And I would buy him like 12, thinking,

00:02:05.827 --> 00:02:07.350
"He wants this, he wants this!"

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.000
- This is me with my children!

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.500
- He hurt my feelings,

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.267
because I would watch him open the gifts

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:14.367
and he would be like, "Eh. Oh."

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.400
And he would get those four
gifts that he asked for,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.260
grab those up and go in his room.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.960
And all the other stuff I
bought is just sitting outside.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.210
- I can beat this. I can beat this.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.214
My kids don't even open them all!

00:02:26.214 --> 00:02:28.020
(audience gasping and giggling)

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.990
There's not that many, like,
you know what I'm saying?

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:31.855
(Taraji sighing)

00:02:31.855 --> 00:02:32.688
They will literally open, once they find

00:02:32.688 --> 00:02:33.959
something they like, they
just go play with it.

00:02:33.959 --> 00:02:34.792
- [Taraji] They're gone.

00:02:34.792 --> 00:02:36.570
- And I'm like, "I'm sorry, I spent a lot

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.370
of time doing this."

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:39.203
- [Taraji] Exactly.

00:02:39.203 --> 00:02:40.474
- Yes.

00:02:40.474 --> 00:02:41.307
- Like, I'm like-

00:02:41.307 --> 00:02:42.660
- These kids, they're so privileged.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.010
- I'm like, "What?" Yeah.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.000
They do not know what it's like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.300
Anyway, let's- and we worked
hard for that, but whatever.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.843
Let's get into a- there's a
lot of therapy here needed.

